IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 7.
-- Part 4, Division 3 (shares): ss 74 to 75: the rights of holders of classes of shares, conversion of shares, and the rights of holders of preference shares.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...): JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)") has the rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings "for a lawyer".
-- A percentage is a NUMBER in per cent (75 means 75 per cent). Treasury shares are disregarded where s 74(1A) says so: the helper `s 74(1A) the percentage ...` does it.

§ `Section 74: rights of holders of classes of shares`

-- (1) the bar on varying or abrogating the rights attached to a class except as the constitution or the 75 per cent default allows. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- Paragraph (a): each of (i) and (ii) that the constitution specifies as necessary must be met, and at least one must be specified; paragraph (b) applies where it specifies neither (fork F-CL1).
-- src:7150 | 74.—(1) Where, in the case of a company the share capital of which
-- src:7151 | is divided into different classes of shares, provision is made in its
-- src:7152 | constitution for authorising the variation or abrogation of the rights
-- src:7153 | attached to any class of shares in the company, the rights attached to
-- src:7154 | the class of shares must not be varied or abrogated except —
-- src:7156 | (a) by either of the following if specified in the constitution as
-- src:7157 | being necessary for such variation or abrogation:
-- src:7159 | (i) the consent of the specified proportion of the holders
-- src:7160 | of the shares of that class;
-- src:7162 | (ii) the sanction of a resolution passed at a separate
-- src:7163 | meeting by the holders in total of not less than the
-- src:7164 | specified proportion of the total number of shares of
-- src:7165 | that class; or
-- src:7167 | (b) where the constitution does not specify the matters
-- src:7168 | mentioned in paragraph (a)(i) and (ii), by the sanction of
-- src:7169 | a resolution passed by the holders in total of not less than
-- src:7170 | 75% of the total number of shares of that class.
@ref s 74(1) (src:7150-7170)
GIVEN `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provision is made in the constitution for authorising the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution specifies the consent of a proportion of the holders of the shares of that class as necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution specifies the sanction of a resolution passed at a separate meeting by a proportion of the holders in total as necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the specified proportion of the holders of the shares of that class has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution passed at a separate meeting by the holders in total of not less than the specified proportion of the total number of shares of that class has sanctioned it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holders who sanctioned it by a resolution hold this percentage of the total number of shares of that class, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1) the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the class is barred` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` AND `provision is made in the constitution for authorising the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares in the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where, in the case of a company the share capital of which is divided into different classes of shares, provision is made in its constitution for authorising the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares" -- another company, or a constitution with no such provision, is not covered
    ELSE (IF    (   `the constitution specifies the consent of a proportion of the holders of the shares of that class as necessary`
                 OR `the constitution specifies the sanction of a resolution passed at a separate meeting by a proportion of the holders in total as necessary`)
             AND ((NOT `the constitution specifies the consent of a proportion of the holders of the shares of that class as necessary`) OR `the consent of the specified proportion of the holders of the shares of that class has been given`)
             AND ((NOT `the constitution specifies the sanction of a resolution passed at a separate meeting by a proportion of the holders in total as necessary`) OR `a resolution passed at a separate meeting by the holders in total of not less than the specified proportion of the total number of shares of that class has sanctioned it`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the rights attached to the class of shares must not be varied or abrogated except -- (a) by either of the following if specified in the constitution as being necessary" -- the exception of paragraph (a) is met
          ELSE (IF    (NOT `the constitution specifies the consent of a proportion of the holders of the shares of that class as necessary`)
                  AND (NOT `the constitution specifies the sanction of a resolution passed at a separate meeting by a proportion of the holders in total as necessary`)
                  AND `the holders who sanctioned it by a resolution hold this percentage of the total number of shares of that class, in per cent` AT LEAST 75
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the constitution does not specify the matters mentioned in paragraph (a)(i) and (ii), by the sanction of a resolution passed by the holders in total of not less than 75% of the total number of shares of that class" -- the exception of paragraph (b) is met
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

DECLARE `s 74 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 74(1) vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares otherwise than as the subsection allows`
    `s 74(5) lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar`

@ref s 74(1) (src:7150-7170)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 74 act`
`s 74(1) a company must not vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares except as the subsection allows` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 74(1) vary or abrogate the rights attached to a class of shares otherwise than as the subsection allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company varied or abrogated the rights attached to a class of shares otherwise than as section 74(1) allows"

-- (1AA) the application to the Court by holders of at least 5 per cent.
-- src:7174 | (1AA) Despite the rights attached to a class of shares in a company
-- src:7175 | having been varied or abrogated in accordance with subsection (1),
-- src:7176 | the holders in total of not less than 5% of the total number of shares of
-- src:7177 | that class may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation
-- src:7178 | cancelled.
@ref s 74(1AA) (src:7174-7178)
GIVEN `the rights attached to the class have been varied or abrogated in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicants hold this percentage of the total number of shares of that class, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1AA) the holders may apply to the Court to have the variation or abrogation cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the rights attached to the class have been varied or abrogated in accordance with subsection (1)` AND `the applicants hold this percentage of the total number of shares of that class, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` AT LEAST 5
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the holders in total of not less than 5% of the total number of shares of that class may apply to the Court" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); the subsection does not say fewer holders may not

-- (1AB) until the Court confirms, the variation or abrogation does not have effect.
-- src:7182 | (1AB) Where an application mentioned in subsection (1AA) is
-- src:7183 | made to the Court, the variation or abrogation of the rights attached to
-- src:7184 | the class of shares does not have effect until confirmed by the Court.
@ref s 74(1AB) (src:7182-7184)
GIVEN `an application mentioned in subsection (1AA) has been made to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has confirmed the variation or abrogation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1AB) the variation or abrogation has not yet taken effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an application mentioned in subsection (1AA) has been made to the Court`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an application mentioned in subsection (1AA) is made to the Court" -- with no application the subsection says nothing
    ELSE (IF `the Court has confirmed the variation or abrogation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not have effect until confirmed by the Court" -- the Court has confirmed it, so the bar is over
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (1A) treasury shares are disregarded.
-- src:7191 | (1A) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (1AA), any of the
-- src:7192 | company’s shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded.
@ref s 74(1A) (src:7191-7192)
GIVEN `the share is held as a treasury share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1A) the share is disregarded for the purposes of subsections (1) and (1AA)` MEANS
    IF `the share is held as a treasury share`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any of the company's shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded" -- another share is not covered

@ref s 74(1A) (src:7191-7192)
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class held by the holders in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 74(1A) the percentage of the total number of shares of the class held by the holders, treasury shares disregarded, in per cent` MEANS
    IF `the total number of issued shares of the class` MINUS `the number of those shares held as treasury shares` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the number of shares of the class held by the holders in question` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY (`the total number of issued shares of the class` MINUS `the number of those shares held as treasury shares`))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no share of the class remains to count once the treasury shares are disregarded; the text gives no percentage of nothing

-- (2) the application is not invalid for the applicants' earlier consent or vote where a material fact was not disclosed.
-- src:7198 | (2) An application mentioned in subsection (1AA) is not invalid by
-- src:7199 | reason of the applicants or any of them having consented to or voted
-- src:7200 | in favour of the resolution for the variation or abrogation if the Court
-- src:7201 | is satisfied that any material fact was not disclosed by the company to
-- src:7202 | those applicants before they so consented or voted.
@ref s 74(2) (src:7198-7202)
GIVEN `the applicants or any of them consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation or abrogation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that a material fact was not disclosed by the company to those applicants before they consented or voted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2) the application is invalid by reason of the applicants having consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the applicants or any of them consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation or abrogation` AND `the Court is satisfied that a material fact was not disclosed by the company to those applicants before they consented or voted`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application mentioned in subsection (1AA) is not invalid by reason of the applicants or any of them having consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation or abrogation if the Court is satisfied that any material fact was not disclosed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Court is satisfied that any material fact was not disclosed" -- the subsection says nothing of an application where no such non-disclosure is shown (fork F-CL2)

-- (3) the time limit: within one month after the consent was given or the resolution passed, or such further time as the Court allows.
-- src:7206 | (3) An application mentioned in subsection (1AA) must be made
-- src:7207 | within one month after the date on which the consent was given or the
-- src:7208 | resolution was passed or such further time as the Court allows, and
-- src:7209 | may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make the
-- src:7210 | application by such one or more of their number as they appoint in
-- src:7211 | writing for the purpose.
@ref s 74(3) (src:7206-7211)
GIVEN `the day the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the Court allows further time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further time the Court allows` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(3) the application is out of time` MEANS
    IF `the application has been made`
    THEN (IF    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the consent was given or the resolution was passed` `the day the application was made` 1 Months
             OR (`the Court allows further time` AND `the day the application was made` AT MOST `the last day of the further time the Court allows`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made within one month after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed or such further time as the Court allows" -- made within the time the text fixes (periods ruling (a); keel convention P4 for a month)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE (IF    `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the consent was given or the resolution was passed` 1 Months
            AND ((NOT `the Court allows further time`) OR `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day of the further time the Court allows`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month after the date ... or such further time as the Court allows" -- the time has not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

@ref s 74(3) (src:7206-7211)
GIVEN `the shareholders entitled to make the application have appointed in writing one or more of their number to make it on their behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(3) the application may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make it by those they appoint` MEANS
    IF `the shareholders entitled to make the application have appointed in writing one or more of their number to make it on their behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they appoint in writing for the purpose" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (4) what the Court does on the application.
-- src:7215 | (4) On the application the Court, after hearing the applicant and any
-- src:7216 | other persons who apply to the Court to be heard and appear to the
-- src:7217 | Court to be interested, may, if satisfied having regard to all the
-- src:7218 | circumstances of the case that the variation or abrogation would
-- src:7219 | unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the
-- src:7220 | applicant, disallow the variation or abrogation, as the case may be,
-- src:7221 | and must, if not so satisfied, confirm it and the decision of the Court is
-- src:7222 | final.
@ref s 74(4) (src:7215-7222)
GIVEN `an application has been made to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons to be heard, is satisfied having regard to all the circumstances that the variation or abrogation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(4) the Court may disallow the variation or abrogation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an application has been made to the Court`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the application the Court" -- with no application the subsection says nothing
    ELSE (IF `the Court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons to be heard, is satisfied having regard to all the circumstances that the variation or abrogation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and must, if not so satisfied, confirm it" -- not satisfied, the Court is to confirm, not disallow

@ref s 74(4) (src:7215-7222)
GIVEN `an application has been made to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons to be heard, is satisfied having regard to all the circumstances that the variation or abrogation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(4) the Court must confirm the variation or abrogation` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an application has been made to the Court`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the application the Court" -- with no application the subsection says nothing
    ELSE (IF `the Court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons to be heard, is satisfied having regard to all the circumstances that the variation or abrogation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if satisfied ... disallow the variation or abrogation" -- satisfied, the Court may disallow; it is not bound to confirm
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 74(4) (src:7215-7222)
GIVEN `the decision is the decision of the Court on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(4) the decision of the Court is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is the decision of the Court on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the decision of the Court is final" -- another decision is not covered

-- (5) the copy of the order within 14 days after the order, and the offence of default.
-- src:7224 | (5) The company must, within 14 days after the making of an order
-- src:7225 | by the Court on any such application, lodge a copy of the order with
-- src:7226 | the Registrar and if default is made in complying with this provision
-- src:7227 | the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:7228 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:7229 | exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 74(5) (src:7224-7229)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order on an application mentioned in subsection (1AA)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the copy was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(5) the company is late in lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court has made an order on an application mentioned in subsection (1AA)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must, within 14 days after the making of an order by the Court on any such application, lodge a copy of the order" -- a failed "after the making of an order" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the order was made` `the day the copy was lodged` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the making of an order by the Court" -- lodged within the 14 days (periods ruling (a))
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the order was made` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 14 days after the making of an order" -- the 14 days have not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

@ref s 74(5) (src:7224-7229)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 74 act`
`s 74(5) a company must lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 74(5) lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the order of the Court with the Registrar within 14 days after the order"

-- src:7224 | (5) The company must, within 14 days after the making of an order
-- src:7225 | by the Court on any such application, lodge a copy of the order with
-- src:7226 | the Registrar and if default is made in complying with this provision
-- src:7227 | the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall
-- src:7228 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:7229 | exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 74(5) (src:7224-7229)
DECLARE `s 74(5) penalty` HAS
    `s 74(5) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 74(5) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 74(5) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 74(5) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 74(5) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 74(5) (src:7224-7229)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 74(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 74(5)`
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "if default is made in complying with this provision the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $2,000 and also to a default penalty" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 74(5) (src:7224-7229)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 74(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 74(5) penalty`
`s 74(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 74(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 74(5)` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 74(5) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 0)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty


-- (6) a pari passu issue of preference shares is deemed a variation unless authorised.
-- src:7231 | (6) The issue by a company of preference shares ranking pari passu
-- src:7232 | with existing preference shares issued by the company is deemed to
-- src:7233 | be a variation of the rights attached to those existing preference shares
-- src:7234 | unless the issue of the firstmentioned shares was authorised by the
-- src:7235 | terms of issue of the existing preference shares or by the constitution
-- src:7240 | of the company in force at the time the existing preference shares
-- src:7241 | were issued.
@ref s 74(6) (src:7231-7241)
GIVEN `the shares issued are preference shares ranking pari passu with existing preference shares issued by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue was authorised by the terms of issue of the existing preference shares or by the constitution of the company in force at the time the existing preference shares were issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(6) the issue is deemed to be a variation of the rights attached to the existing preference shares` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the shares issued are preference shares ranking pari passu with existing preference shares issued by the company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The issue by a company of preference shares ranking pari passu with existing preference shares issued by the company" -- another issue is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the issue was authorised by the terms of issue of the existing preference shares or by the constitution of the company in force at the time the existing preference shares were issued`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to be a variation of the rights attached to those existing preference shares unless the issue of the firstmentioned shares was authorised by the terms of issue" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (7) altering the manner of variation is itself a variation.
-- src:7245 | (7) For the purposes of this section, the alteration of any provision
-- src:7246 | in the constitution of a company which affects or relates to the
-- src:7247 | manner in which the rights attaching to the shares of any class may be
-- src:7248 | varied or abrogated is deemed to be a variation or abrogation of the
-- src:7249 | rights attached to the shares of that class.
@ref s 74(7) (src:7245-7249)
GIVEN `the alteration of a provision in the constitution affects or relates to the manner in which the rights attaching to the shares of a class may be varied or abrogated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(7) the alteration is deemed to be a variation or abrogation of the rights attached to the shares of the class` MEANS
    IF `the alteration of a provision in the constitution affects or relates to the manner in which the rights attaching to the shares of a class may be varied or abrogated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the alteration of any provision in the constitution of a company which affects or relates to the manner in which the rights attaching to the shares of any class may be varied or abrogated" -- another alteration is not covered

-- (8) saving of relief under section 216.
-- src:7253 | (8) This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the
-- src:7254 | rights of any person to obtain relief under section 216.
@ref s 74(8) (src:7253-7254)
GIVEN `the right is a right of a person to obtain relief under section 216` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(8) section 74 limits or derogates from the right` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right of a person to obtain relief under section 216`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not operate so as to limit or derogate from the rights of any person to obtain relief under section 216"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the rights of any person to obtain relief under section 216" -- another right is not covered

§ `Section 74A: conversion of shares`

-- (1) the provision in the constitution. "Subject to this section and sections 64A and 75": delegated.
-- src:7258 | 74A.—(1) Subject to this section and sections 64A and 75, a
-- src:7259 | company the share capital of which is divided into different classes of
-- src:7260 | shares may make provision in its constitution to authorise the
-- src:7261 | conversion of one class of shares into another class of shares.
@ref s 74A(1) (src:7258-7261)
GIVEN `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this section, section 64A or section 75 forbids the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(1) the company may make provision in its constitution to authorise the conversion of one class of shares into another class` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the share capital of the company is divided into different classes of shares`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company the share capital of which is divided into different classes of shares" -- another company is not covered
    ELSE (IF `this section, section 64A or section 75 forbids the provision`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (delegated): "Subject to this section and sections 64A and 75" -- the answer sits in those provisions (fork F-X2)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (2) a public company converting by special resolution "only if" the constitution permits B and sets out its rights.
-- src:7265 | (2) A public company may convert one class of shares (A) into
-- src:7266 | another class of shares (B) by special resolution only if the
-- src:7267 | constitution of the public company —
-- src:7269 | (a) permits B to be issued; and
-- src:7271 | (b) sets out the rights attached to B.
@ref s 74A(2) (src:7265-7271)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conversion is made by special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the public company permits the class of shares converted into to be issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the public company sets out the rights attached to the class of shares converted into` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(2) the public company may convert one class of shares into another class by special resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR (NOT `the conversion is made by special resolution`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may convert one class of shares (A) into another class of shares (B) by special resolution" -- a private company, or a conversion by another means, is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the constitution of the public company permits the class of shares converted into to be issued` AND `the constitution of the public company sets out the rights attached to the class of shares converted into`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by special resolution only if the constitution of the public company -- (a) permits B to be issued; and (b) sets out the rights attached to B" -- an "only if" the constitution does not meet

-- (3) a private company's conversion by notice.
-- src:7275 | (3) A private company may convert shares from one class to
-- src:7276 | another by lodging a notice of conversion in the prescribed form with
-- src:7277 | the Registrar.
@ref s 74A(3) (src:7275-7277)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice of conversion in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(3) the private company may convert shares from one class to another by lodging the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `a notice of conversion in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may convert shares from one class to another by lodging a notice of conversion in the prescribed form with the Registrar" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (4) the conversion by a private company does not take effect until the register is updated.
-- src:7281 | (4) A conversion of shares by a private company on or after
-- src:7282 | 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of
-- src:7283 | members of the company is updated by the Registrar under
-- src:7284 | section 196A(5).
@ref s 74A(4) (src:7281-7284)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the conversion` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(4) the conversion has not yet taken effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR `the day of the conversion` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A conversion of shares by a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a public company or a conversion before 3 January 2016 is not covered (periods ruling (c); fork F-X1)
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- the register has been updated, so the bar is over
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (5) section 74 applies to a conversion that varies or abrogates class rights.
-- src:7288 | (5) Section 74 applies where a conversion of shares undertaken by a
-- src:7289 | company involves a variation or an abrogation of the rights attached
-- src:7290 | to any class of shares in the company.
@ref s 74A(5) (src:7288-7290)
GIVEN `the conversion of shares undertaken by the company involves a variation or an abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(5) section 74 applies to the conversion` MEANS
    IF `the conversion of shares undertaken by the company involves a variation or an abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 74 applies where a conversion of shares undertaken by a company involves a variation or an abrogation of the rights attached to any class of shares" -- a conversion that involves neither is not covered; the subsection does not say section 74 does not apply

-- (6) no conversion into a redeemable preference share.
-- src:7297 | (6) Despite anything in this section, a share that is not a redeemable
-- src:7298 | preference share when issued cannot afterwards be converted into a
-- src:7299 | redeemable preference share.
@ref s 74A(6) (src:7297-7299)
GIVEN `the share was a redeemable preference share when it was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74A(6) the share may be converted into a redeemable preference share` MEANS
    IF `the share was a redeemable preference share when it was issued`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a share that is not a redeemable preference share when issued cannot afterwards be converted" -- a share that was one when issued is not covered by this subsection
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a share that is not a redeemable preference share when issued cannot afterwards be converted into a redeemable preference share"

§ `Section 75: rights of holders of preference shares to be set out in the constitution`

-- (1) the bar on allotting or converting into preference shares unless the five rights are set out. JUST TRUE is barred.
-- src:7306 | 75.—(1) No company may allot any preference shares or convert
-- src:7307 | any issued shares into preference shares unless there are set out in its
-- src:7308 | constitution the rights of the holders of those shares with respect to
-- src:7309 | repayment of capital, participation in surplus assets and profits,
-- src:7310 | cumulative or non‑cumulative dividends, voting and priority of
-- src:7311 | payment of capital and dividend in relation to other shares or other
-- src:7312 | classes of preference shares.
@ref s 75(1) (src:7306-7312)
GIVEN `the company allots preference shares or converts issued shares into preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to repayment of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to participation in surplus assets and profits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to cumulative or non-cumulative dividends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to priority of payment of capital and dividend in relation to other shares or other classes of preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(1) the company is barred from allotting the preference shares or converting issued shares into them` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company allots preference shares or converts issued shares into preference shares`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "allot any preference shares or convert any issued shares into preference shares" -- another act is not covered
    ELSE (IF    `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to repayment of capital`
            AND `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to participation in surplus assets and profits`
            AND `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to cumulative or non-cumulative dividends`
            AND `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to voting`
            AND `the constitution sets out the rights of the holders with respect to priority of payment of capital and dividend in relation to other shares or other classes of preference shares`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No company may allot any preference shares or convert any issued shares into preference shares unless there are set out in its constitution the rights of the holders of those shares" -- the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

DECLARE `s 75 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 75(1) allot preference shares or convert issued shares into preference shares without setting out the rights of the holders in the constitution`

@ref s 75(1) (src:7306-7312)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 75 act`
`s 75(1) a company must not allot preference shares or convert issued shares into them unless the rights of the holders are set out in the constitution` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 75(1) allot preference shares or convert issued shares into preference shares without setting out the rights of the holders in the constitution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company allotted preference shares or converted issued shares into preference shares without setting out the rights of the holders in its constitution"

-- (2) the offence of default.
-- src:7316 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:7317 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:7318 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:7319 | $2,000.
@ref s 75(2) (src:7316-7319)
DECLARE `s 75(2) penalty` HAS
    `s 75(2) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 75(2) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 75(2) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 75(2) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 75(2) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 75(2) (src:7316-7319)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 75` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 75`
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 75(2) (src:7316-7319)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 75` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 75(2) penalty`
`s 75(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 75(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 75` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 75(2) penalty` OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

